;; demos/scenarios/clinic-decade/config.edn -- the vendoring
;; batch 2 rider (AR-VB2-R, 2026-08-07): the scenarios/ home's first
;; entry, a busy weekday mix across the twelve everyday-ambulatory and
;; acute modules vendored across the vendoring arc's first two batches
;; (sore_throat/sinusitis/bronchitis/asthma/ear_infections/urinary_tract_
;; infections/sleep_apnea/fibromyalgia/dementia/appendicitis/
;; total_joint_replacement/sepsis) plus a five-minute arrival gap for a
;; steady, busy stream. `:module-initial-attributes` seeds every
;; total-joint-replacement walk to the knee variant (ADR-0033 AR-1's own
;; attachment rule) so that closure's own content lands without relying
;; on its default attribute distribution. Landed VERBATIM from the
;; design channel's own authored copy (AR-VB2-R) -- see this directory's
;; own README.md for the runnable command and the live-probe result.
{:pathway {:name "clinic-decade" :steps []}
 :arrival-gap 5
 :modules ["sore_throat" "sinusitis" "bronchitis" "asthma" "ear_infections"
           "urinary_tract_infections" "sleep_apnea" "fibromyalgia" "dementia"
           "appendicitis" "total_joint_replacement" "sepsis"]
 :module-assignment [{:module-id "sore_throat" :weight 15}
                      {:module-id "sinusitis" :weight 12}
                      {:module-id "bronchitis" :weight 10}
                      {:module-id "asthma" :weight 10}
                      {:module-id "ear_infections" :weight 8}
                      {:module-id "urinary_tract_infections" :weight 8}
                      {:module-id "sleep_apnea" :weight 7}
                      {:module-id "fibromyalgia" :weight 6}
                      {:module-id "dementia" :weight 6}
                      {:module-id "appendicitis" :weight 6}
                      {:module-id "total_joint_replacement" :weight 6}
                      {:module-id "sepsis" :weight 6}]
 :module-initial-attributes {"total_joint_replacement" {:total-joint-replacement/joint-replacement "knee"}}
 ;; ARC 3A PART 4 (ADR-0173 ruling D1's commit 2, 2026-08-26): the
 ;; demographic fold, TURNED ON. This is the opt-in -- `:persons` absent
 ;; is the byte-identical path, and this file is one of the six corpora
 ;; that stop taking it.
 ;;
 ;; `:count` IS TWICE THE ARRIVAL COUNT, and both the shape and the
 ;; factor are measurements rather than preferences. With `:persons`
 ;; present an arrival BINDS to a person, and a repeat arrival of
 ;; somebody already registered queues NOTHING (ADR-0173's own first
 ;; tabled deviation: a second `:admission` for a discharged patient
 ;; violates `admission-only-when-new`). So a small pool silently
 ;; deletes clinical content -- probed at `:count` 50 against 200
 ;; arrivals, only 50 patients registered and three quarters of this
 ;; scenario's own module walks never happened.
 ;;
 ;; One person per arrival is not enough either, and the generator-side
 ;; COVERAGE GATE is what said so: at `:count` 200 the birthday paradox
 ;; still makes better than a third of the arrivals repeats, and the
 ;; module coverage that thinned took this scenario's only
 ;; module-compiled `:admission`/`:discharge` pair with it --
 ;; `gated-runs-collectively-produce-every-emittable-event-type` went
 ;; red on exactly those two kinds. At twice the arrival count the
 ;; collision rate drops enough that both come back.
 ;;
 ;; `:years` IS TWENTY, not the ten `ehrt.sim.run/default-person-years`
 ;; would give, and that is a measurement too: at 10 years this
 ;; population produced ZERO occupational injuries (the hazard is
 ;; conditioned on `:employed` person-years, and most of a ten-year walk
 ;; is not), so the clinical hook would have been declared and never
 ;; witnessed. At 20 it fires. A run's own log therefore extends to the
 ;; PERSON horizon, well past its clinical content -- that is what a
 ;; demographic timeline is, and this scenario's own README carries the
 ;; re-witnessed figures.
 :persons {:count 400 :years 20}

 ;; ARC 3B SWEEP 1 (ADR-0174 rulings A1/E1, 2026-08-26): the ENCOUNTER
 ;; HORIZON, LIFTED. This is the opt-in -- `:encounters` absent is the
 ;; byte-identical path, and this file is one of the six corpora that
 ;; stop taking it.
 ;;
 ;; IT CHANGES WHAT THE PARAGRAPH ABOVE MEANS, and that is said here
 ;; rather than left for a reader to notice. A repeat arrival no longer
 ;; queues NOTHING: with no encounter open it opens a SECOND one, on the
 ;; same patient and the same MRN, which is what an MPI under test needs
 ;; to see. So the pool-sizing argument above is no longer about
 ;; DELETED clinical content -- the content a collision used to cost is
 ;; now a return visit -- but the sizing itself is kept unchanged, for
 ;; two reasons: the coverage gate it was tuned against still reads the
 ;; same population, and re-tuning a pool in the same commit that lifts
 ;; the horizon would leave any corpus delta with two possible causes.
 ;;
 ;; WHAT DOES NOT CHANGE: a repeat arrival landing while the patient's
 ;; first encounter is still OPEN still opens nothing (`decide
 ;; :repeat-arrival`), and one landing on a `:merged` or `:expired`
 ;; patient still opens nothing either. Both terminals stay absorbing.
 :encounters true

 ;; ARC 3B SWEEP 2 (ADR-0174 section 2(c) plus ruling C, 2026-08-27): the
 ;; BED-STATUS CYCLE, ON. A vacated bed goes `:dirty`, then `:cleaning`,
 ;; then `:ready`, at the pace each ward's own `:turnaround-minutes`
 ;; declares, and `allocate` is gated on `:ready`.
 ;;
 ;; WHAT IT CHANGES HERE IS ALMOST NOTHING, and that is worth stating
 ;; rather than leaving a reader to expect otherwise. This scenario
 ;; produces NO bed-ready transfers at all -- measured, at both gated
 ;; seeds and at the demo seed -- because its ambulatory decade never
 ;; boards anybody, so the discharge-to-relief coupling the cycle moves
 ;; has nothing here to move. What the opt-in DOES buy is the
 ;; `:bed-status-change` stream and its ADT^A20 traffic for its handful
 ;; of admissions, which is what makes a bed board of this corpus show a
 ;; room being turned over rather than a bed blinking from occupied to
 ;; empty. It takes the key for the same reason it takes `:encounters`:
 ;; a scenario a reader runs by hand and a gated corpus must not
 ;; disagree about what is in them.
 :bed-cycle true

 ;; ARC 3B SWEEP 3 (ADR-0174 section 2(b) plus ruling C, 2026-08-27):
 ;; SCHEDULING, ON. Arrivals split scheduled-vs-walk-in, appointments
 ;; carry their own outcome, and a discharge may book a return visit.
 ;;
 ;; :scheduled-fraction IS HIGH HERE, and it is the one sub-key this
 ;; scenario genuinely disagrees with ed-tuesday about. A DECADE OF
 ;; AMBULATORY CARE IS BOOKED TRAFFIC: people make appointments and keep
 ;; them, and the walk-in tail is the minority. 0.70 says roughly seven
 ;; arrivals in ten arrived against a booking; ed-tuesday's single ED
 ;; shift says 0.15 for exactly the opposite reason. ADR-0174 section
 ;; 2(b) names the six sub-keys and states NO VALUES for any of them, so
 ;; every number here is this session's own choice, made on clinical
 ;; grounds and disclosed as a choice rather than cited as a default
 ;; that does not exist.
 ;;
 ;; The lead times and the follow-up interval are LONGER than the ED's
 ;; for the same reason the horizon is 3650 days and not 90: a clinic
 ;; books weeks out and follows up in months, an ED books days out and
 ;; follows up in weeks.
 ;;
 ;; THE CAPACITY MARGIN, MEASURED BEFORE THE OPT-IN AND AFTER IT.
 ;; `:exhausted` HALTS a run (ADR-0174 section 2(c)'s own withdrawn
 ;; premise), so this opt-in owes a measured margin against the union of
 ;; beds the four rungs can reach. This scenario is nowhere near it and
 ;; the numbers say so plainly -- worst home ward, both seeds, before
 ;; AND after: 13 of 16 free (81.3%) at seed 424242, 14 of 16 (87.5%) at
 ;; seed 5. The ladder never reaches rung 3 in either. Sparse traffic
 ;; over ten years is what makes this scenario the roomy one; the
 ;; measurement is recorded anyway, because a margin nobody measured is
 ;; the thing the ADR's withdrawn premise cost sweep 2 three rejected
 ;; configurations to learn.
 :scheduling {:scheduled-fraction 0.70
              :lead-time-days [3 21]
              :no-show-rate 0.15
              :reschedule-rate 0.10
              :cancel-rate 0.08
              :follow-up {:rate 0.35 :interval-days [30 120]}}
 :module-horizon-days 3650}
